    "layout": {
      "x": 5440,
      "y": 0,
      "w": 480,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "blue",
      "text": "Layout rules (sancus/app.css)\n\n• One 12-column grid on every screen. Tiles in a row share a height, so edges line up whatever the data does.\n• Lists in tiles are capped (5 on Home, 3 in side tiles) and end in \"See all\" with a count.\n• Names truncate with …, amounts never do.\n• Every tile has an empty state the same size (see 03).\n• 12 cols above 1100px, 6 cols to 720px, 1 col below.\n• Pay flow: form on the left, the same summary panel on the right on every step."
    },
    "teammate": {
      "x": 5440,
      "y": 720,
      "w": 480,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "yellow",
      "text": "From the GlobalPay admin mockups\n\n• Overview chart + Add funds → Home balance tile, 04 Add money\n• Activity tabs, Approvals with detail panel → 09, 10\n• Recipients → Pay step 1 (05)\n• Payment methods → Settings › Where you can pay (17)\n• Employee profile, local QR spending, Issue card → 12–15\n• x402 endpoints, Assistant → 16\n• Approval threshold, workspace → 17\n• Left out: \"Convert\" (unclear what it converts) and the network picker on Home (chain stays on the security section)."
    },
    "readme": {
      "x": 960,
      "y": 7580,
      "w": 520,
      "size": "m",
      "fill": "teal",
      "text": "How to read these\n\n• Demo company: Café Paulista Ltda (Brazil), owner Maya. Numbers add up across screens: $10,000 in, Lumen $1,000, Northwind $2,000 pending, Juliana $100.80, Ana's card $100 and Pix QR $10, 3 approvals waiting ($2,620.05).\n• Built on docs/brand tokens + components, plus sancus/app.css for layout.\n• Rails other than USDC carry the Simulated pill.\n• Press Play on any desktop screen to click through."
    },
